I left out the logging and metadata-fetch requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability, and calling `metadata.internal.example` needs an HTTP capability. Adding either import would widen the node's authority beyond its declared grant, and the metadata call would also send the untrusted message text to an external host. If operations needs this behavior, it should be granted as a separate node with its own `with` clause.

